.TH BASEFWX 7 "August 2026" "BaseFWX 3.8.0-dev1" "BaseFWX Manual"
.SH NAME
basefwx \- C++ cryptographic codec library and container family
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <basefwx/basefwx.hpp>

pkg-config --cflags --libs basefwx

find_package(basefwx 3.8 CONFIG REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(app PRIVATE basefwx::basefwxcpp)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
BaseFWX is a cryptographic codec toolkit. It protects files and byte streams.
It is not a network transport by itself and it does not provide anonymity by
itself.
.PP
Applications such as YUME use BaseFWX as an inner cryptographic and encoding
layer. The C++ library provides authenticated encryption, password hardening,
post-quantum key encapsulation when built with liboqs support, and live stream
framing.
.PP
The Debian packaging in this source tree ships the C++ CLI, shared library,
and development files as separate binary packages from one source package.
It does not install the Python or Java modules.
.SH BASIC FLOW
.nf
+--------------------------------+
|  CALLER                        |
|  CLI / library / YUME          |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        | password, bytes, options
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  BASEFWX CORE                  |
|  KDF, keys, AEAD, metadata     |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        | encrypted container
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  OUTPUT FORMAT                 |
|  file or packet                |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        | stored or transported
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  DECODER                       |
|  verifies before release       |
+--------------------------------+
.fi
.PP
The caller supplies plaintext bytes and a password or key context. BaseFWX
derives or unwraps encryption keys, encrypts and authenticates the payload,
and writes a format another BaseFWX implementation can parse.
.PP
On decode, BaseFWX reads authenticated metadata, derives or unwraps the same
keys, verifies integrity, and releases plaintext only after verification
passes.
.SH CODEC FAMILIES
.TP
.B fwxAES
AES-GCM file encryption with metadata and optional wrappers.
.TP
.B pb512 / b512
Authenticated AES-256-GCM text payloads with password or optional master-key
wrapping, plus related file modes. Current writers emit payload version 3;
version 2 decode requires
.BR BASEFWX_ALLOW_LEGACY_TEXT_V2=1
for trusted-data recovery.
.TP
.B livecipher
Packetized stream encryption for pipes and transport use.
.TP
.B keywrap / pq
Password and master-key wrapping helpers, including ML-KEM-768/1024 when liboqs
support is enabled.
.TP
.B n10 / b512
Maintained reversible text and binary encodings.
.SH RETIRED COMPATIBILITY FORMATS
b256, A512, Bi512, Uhash513, the kFM/kFA carrier codecs, and the jMG media
cipher are retired. A default build compiles and installs none of them: their
implementations, CLI commands, tests, and benchmarks are all absent, and
.B BASEFWX_HAS_RETIRED_MEDIA
is 0 in the installed CMake and pkg-config metadata.
.PP
Configuring with
.B -DBASEFWX_ENABLE_RETIRED_MEDIA=ON
produces a compatibility library that carries them. The historical switch name
is retained for build-script compatibility. That profile exists to read retired
data that already exists. It preserves the historical APIs, formats, and bytes
unchanged, and receives security, correctness, and existing-data compatibility
fixes only; no new retired formats or features are planned.
.PP
The switch decides what gets compiled, so it cannot re-enable these formats in a
library that was built without them. Link against a compatibility build of the
same BaseFWX version that wrote the file. Protect new media with
.B fwxAES
instead, which gives it the same AEAD guarantees as any other file.
.SH FILE CONTAINERS
.nf
+--------------------------------+
|  PLAINTEXT FILE                |
|  bytes from disk or stdin      |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  KDF AND KEY SETUP             |
|  Argon2id or PBKDF2            |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  AEAD ENCRYPTION               |
|  AES-256-GCM + metadata        |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        | ===>
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  BASEFWX CONTAINER             |
|  FWX1 / heavy / encoded form   |
+--------------------------------+
.fi
.PP
At a high level, encrypted file containers carry authenticated metadata and
encrypted payload bytes:
.nf
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  BASEFWX ENCRYPTED CONTAINER                                         |
|                                                                      |
|  magic/version | KDF parameters | wrap data | metadata | ciphertext  |
|                                                                      |
|  metadata is authenticated; payload releases after verification      |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
.fi
.PP
Exact byte layout depends on the selected codec family. Use the public API
to read and write containers instead of hand-parsing container fields.
.SH LIVE STREAMS
.nf
+--------------------------------+
|  PRODUCER                      |
|  file, ffmpeg, app bytes       |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  LIVE ENCRYPTOR                |
|  start, update, finalize       |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        | ===>
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  LIVE PACKETS                  |
|  ordered AES-GCM frames        |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  LIVE DECRYPTOR                |
|  verifies packet sequence      |
+--------------------------------+
.fi
.PP
Live mode emits packetized frames, keeping memory bounded for pipes,
sockets, and transport integrations. Receivers must process frames in order
and finalize before treating the stream as complete.
.SH YUME INTEGRATION
.nf
+--------------------------------+
|  YUME STREAM                   |
|  logical app connection        |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  BASEFWX INNER CRYPTO          |
|  AES / Argon2id / ML-KEM       |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        | ===>
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  YUME CARRIER                  |
|  TLS 1.3 + YUME frames         |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  YUMED SERVER                  |
|  unwraps inner stream data     |
+--------------------------------+
.fi
.PP
For packaged YUME builds, the yume binary links against libbasefwx.so.4
through the libbasefwx-dev build package and the libbasefwx4 runtime package.
.SH PACKAGE LAYOUT
.nf
+--------------------------------+
|  basefwx                       |
|  command-line frontend         |
+--------------------------------+
        |
        v
+--------------------------------+
|  libbasefwx4                   |
|  runtime shared library        |
+--------------------------------+
        ^
        |
+--------------------------------+
|  libbasefwx-dev                |
|  headers and build metadata    |
+--------------------------------+
        ^
        |
+--------------------------------+
|  yume                          |
|  links to libbasefwx.so.4      |
+--------------------------------+
.fi
.PP
Local development builds may use a prepared vendor liboqs staging directory
to keep ML-KEM-768/1024 available. Debian archive builds should use a normal
packaged liboqs-dev dependency instead of embedding liboqs into BaseFWX.
.SH FAILURE MODEL
BaseFWX fails closed. A wrong password, changed ciphertext, missing PQ support
for a PQ-required container, or a truncated live stream fails instead of
releasing unauthenticated plaintext. A compatibility build applies the same rule
to retired carrier input that is not a BaseFWX carrier.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/include/basefwx/
C++ public headers.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/<multiarch>/libbasefwx.so.4
BaseFWX runtime shared library.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/<multiarch>/cmake/basefwx/
CMake package files.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/<multiarch>/pkgconfig/basefwx.pc
pkg-config metadata.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/libbasefwx4/EXPLAINED.md.gz
Extended overview with reusable diagrams.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR basefwx (1)
.PP
YUME is a separate sibling project that can link against
.BR libbasefwx ;
its manual pages (if installed) are
